WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.099
Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:02.120
I don't know what today's video is about.

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:05.689
I'm on a social media hiatus right now, it
turns out it's very difficult for me to hiate

00:00:05.689 --> 00:00:08.300
from social media, but I'm on the hiatus to
write a book.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.890
Like, I've been "working" on a novel for the
last four years, but I'm trying to, like,

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:14.130
take the quotation marks out of that "working".

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:17.500
But like, when I'm really into a story, it's
hard to think about anything else, so I'm

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.680
just, like, sitting here thinking about things
that I can't tell you about.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.020
Anyway, I think it's going well, but who knows,
I've been wrong before.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.690
I know there were things I was supposed to
talk about.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:25.690
Oh, right, NerdCon!

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:29.160
Hank, NerdCon: Stories is just like a week
and a half away in the beautiful city of Minneapolis.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.579
There's a great bunch of storytellers coming,
but the relevant thing here, Hank, is that

00:00:32.579 --> 00:00:36.850
somehow or another, I agreed to a race car
race with my friend, Maggie.

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.030
You know, Maggie Stevater.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:39.030
Stivater?

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.030
Stream Water?

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:41.289
You know, Maggie, who wrote all of those great
books.

00:00:41.289 --> 00:00:44.670
Apparently, it's Stiefvater, Steve like the
name, otter like the mammal.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:49.649
So separate from NerdCon, she and I are going
to be racing in actual race cars on an actual

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:55.139
race car track on October 9th at 7:30 at Princeton
Speedway outside of Minneapolis.

00:00:55.139 --> 00:00:58.589
It's 5 bucks at the door, all the proceeds
go to this charity Drivers Edge, and I have

00:00:58.589 --> 00:01:02.460
to wear, like, a helmet and a fire suit in
case my car catches on fire, and I'm going

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:03.460
to lose.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:08.140
Oh, also, there's flowing water on Mars occasionally,
apparently, and it's very exciting, and the

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:11.159
SciShow people got so excited, they made,
like, shirts and posters.

00:01:11.159 --> 00:01:14.930
Hank, I feel vicariously very happy for you
whenever there's big Mars news like this,

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:19.930
but you what's so exciting that we haven't
taken a second to just be psyched about lately?

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:21.180
Flowing water on Earth!

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.270
Earth, man!

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:23.900
What a planet!

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:27.000
Sarah says I should show you how my tattoo
is doing, so I'm going to do that now.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Don't get alarmed, Hank.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.409
I'm just, you know, taking off my shirt.

00:01:29.409 --> 00:01:30.409
Still there a little bit.

00:01:30.409 --> 00:01:31.409
What else?

00:01:31.409 --> 00:01:32.409
Oh!

00:01:32.409 --> 00:01:33.409
The wall!

00:01:33.409 --> 00:01:34.409
So many people, Hank, were complaining about
the blank, blue wall that I finally put up

00:01:34.409 --> 00:01:35.409
my wall stuff.

00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:38.820
We've got Woody Guthrie and his guitar, a
big Willy and a medium-sized me and a puppy-sized

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:42.299
